 complex queries, break them down into subtasks and use the tool multiple times.\\n5. Use it as a starting point for complex tasks, then refine with specialized tools.\\n6. Verify important information from its responses.\\n"}, \'require_llm_engine\': True}, \'Local_Wikipedia_Search_Tool\': {\'tool_name\': \'Local_Wikipedia_Search_Tool\', \'tool_description\': \'A Wikipedia search tool that returns the most relevant Wikipedia passages for a query.\', \'tool_version\': \'1.0.0\', \'input_types\': {\'query\': \'str - The search query, e.g. an entity name and the fact to find.\'}, \'output_type\': \'str - The top Wikipedia passages, each with its article title.\', \'demo_commands\': [{\'command\': \'execution = tool.execute(query="Citibank founding year")\', \'description\': \'Find the year Citibank was founded.\'}, {\'command\': \'execution = tool.execute(query="President of the United States in 1812")\', \'description\': \'Find who was U.S. president in a given year.\'}], \'user_metadata\': {\'limitations\': \'\\n1. Searches a fixed 2018 English Wikipedia snapshot, not the live web.\\n2. Returns the top passages for the query; it does not summarize them.\\n3. Each passage is a 100-word chunk, so one search may not contain the full answer.\\n\', \'best_practices\': \'\\n1. Use this tool to look up facts about people, places, organizations, events, and dates.\\n2. Search for one entity or fact at a time; for multi-hop questions, search again with the entity found in the previous step.\\n3. Use short, specific queries such as "Citibank founding year" rather than full questions.\\n\'}, \'require_llm_engine\': False}, \'Python_Code_Generator_Tool\': {\'tool_name\': \'Python_Code_Generator_Tool\', \'tool_description\': \'A tool that generates and executes simple Python code snippets for basic arithmetical calculations and math-related problems. The generated code runs in a highly restricted environment with only basic mathematical operations available.\', \'tool_version\':